      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: incomplete—event evidence unavailable\n\nI verified the relevant work order and Pending Close cutoff, but **cannot determine whether an event was created afterward** from the records available to my authorized role.\n\n| Required item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order | **WO-2025-09-004** — Cooler Plate Pack, Modine Racine |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25**, `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not verifiable from accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot conclude without the event type, timing, and recorded status |\n\nThe timestamp above is reproduced exactly; the source provides no timezone offset.\n\n### Oracle policy\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting”** (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that new transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period **will not be staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting** until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, even if in error. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing.\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary, non-exempt transaction created after the cutoff for September or an earlier period should be held rather than processed. I cannot verify whether the actual recorded status follows that rule.\n\n### Evidence limitation and disposition\n\nThe accessible Task records contain work orders, cost periods, and the policy excerpt, but **no cost-event rows**. That omission does **not** establish that no late event exists. Supporting event records are restricted to the records-custodian role; I requested authorized evidence and escalated the gap.\n\nThe audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_3e82b3b683ca/audit-report.json` and submitted with status **needs_evidence**. **No database records were changed.**",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
